sequenceDiagram
    accTitle: Implemented Paper Async Observation Selection
    accDescr: The static runner advances the simulator serially. Each control step stores an observation snapshot. On a new request it selects t minus n-prime history, falling back to the current observation when history is insufficient, and executes the first n predicted actions.
    participant runner as Static runner
    participant simulator as Native simulator
    participant engine as Cosmos engine
    runner->>simulator: reset episode and settle
    simulator-->>runner: observation and current instruction
    runner->>engine: reset episode identity
    loop Until success or budget
        runner->>runner: append snapshot at control step t
        opt No actions queued
            runner->>runner: select snapshot at t minus n-prime
            Note over runner: Use current snapshot if history is insufficient
            runner->>engine: infer_chunk with images and proprio from same snapshot
            engine-->>runner: H predicted actions
            runner->>runner: queue first n actions
        end
        runner->>simulator: step one action
        simulator-->>runner: observation, success, terminal
        runner->>runner: count one completed control step
    end
    Note over runner,engine: Serial history abstraction, inference timing is measured separately
